    "text": "the-hospitalist.org\nwebsite\nValdosta\nThe Care and Feeding of Your Nocturnist: A Field Guide for Diurnals\nBy Arnold Facklam, NP, FHM,\n1 days agoIt is a curious feature of modern medical ecosystems that diurnal creatures—those brisk, tie-wearing types or business casual disciples of daylight—persist in misunderstanding the elusive nocturnist. We dwell where owls roost and fluorescent hallway lights flicker. Our circadian rhythms, along with being sleep-deprived, are like jazz: unpredictable and oddly poetic.",
